steps.message:
## Diagnosis

Comment bodies are rendered by `HtmlTextView`, whose links are driven by `LocalLinkMovementMethod` (set in `HtmlTextView.setHtml`). Its `onTouchEvent` unconditionally called `link[0].onClick(widget)` on every `ACTION_UP` over a link — with no regard for whether the gesture had already been consumed as a long press.

Meanwhile `CommentsRecyclerViewAdapter.ItemViewHolder` attaches `commentBody.setOnLongClickListener(...)` which opens the comment menu. On a long tap over a URL, the sequence was:

1. `ACTION_DOWN` → `View` posts the long-press check.
2. After the timeout → `OnLongClickListener` fires → comment menu opens.
3. Finger lifts → `ACTION_UP` still reaches the movement method → `URLSpan.onClick` → `Utils.openLinkMaybeHN(...)` → the URL opens too.

## Fix

**`HtmlTextView.java`** — track whether a long press was consumed in the current gesture: reset the flag on `ACTION_DOWN`, set it in an overridden `performLongClick()` when the long click is handled, and expose `hasPerformedLongPress()`.

**`LocalLinkMovementMethod.java`** — on `ACTION_UP` over a link, clear the selection and only invoke `link[0].onClick(widget)` when the gesture was *not* a long press:

```java
if (action == MotionEvent.ACTION_UP) {
    Selection.removeSelection(buffer);
    // Don't open the link if the touch turned into a long press, since the
    // long press already triggered another action (like the comment menu)
    if (!isLongPress(widget, event)) {
        link[0].onClick(widget);
    }
} else if (action == MotionEvent.ACTION_DOWN) { ... }
```

`isLongPress` first consults `HtmlTextView.hasPerformedLongPress()` (exact signal), and falls back to a timing check (`eventTime - downTime >= ViewConfiguration.getLongPressTimeout()`) guarded by `widget.isLongClickable()`. The `isLongClickable()` guard preserves existing behaviour for text views that have no long-press action (e.g. dialog/story body text), where a slow tap should still open the link.

Normal short taps on links are unaffected (flag false, elapsed time under the timeout), so link opening, link selection highlight on press, and comment collapsing all continue to work. `./gradlew clean assembleDebug` completes with **BUILD SUCCESSFUL**.

